---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const P1 = `PROCEDURE addTax(price)
{
  RETURN(price + price * 0.1)
}

DISPLAY(addTax(100))
DISPLAY(addTax(addTax(100)))`;
const P2 = `PROCEDURE band(n)
{
  IF(n >= 90)
  {
    RETURN("A")
  }
  ELSE
  {
    IF(n >= 80)
    {
      RETURN("B")
    }
    ELSE
    {
      RETURN("C")
    }
  }
}

scores <- [95, 80, 79]
FOR EACH s IN scores
{
  DISPLAY(band(s))
}`;
const P3 = `PROCEDURE mystery(a, b)
{
  IF(a > b)
  {
    RETURN(a)
  }
  RETURN(b)
}

DISPLAY(mystery(3, 9))
DISPLAY(mystery(9, 3))
DISPLAY(mystery(4, 4))`;
const RefCard = `PROCEDURE procName(p1, p2)     define a procedure
{
  ...
  RETURN(expression)           hand a value back AND exit immediately
}

result <- procName(a, b)       call it and capture what it returns
procName(a, b)                 call it and ignore what it returns

a <- expression                assign a COPY of the result
DISPLAY(expression)            show it, FOLLOWED BY A SPACE
=  is equality.  <- is assignment.  No == anywhere.

IF(condition) { } ELSE { }     the only two selection forms`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Pseudocode Challenge: Tracing Procedures</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>Three traces. All three are about what a procedure hands back &mdash; the thing the multiple-choice section asks about most often once procedures appear.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Do this on paper.</b> There is nothing to run. On exam day you
            get this notation printed and no computer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="reference">
          <h2>Reference Card</h2>

          <Code code={RefCard} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam Notation — what you have so far" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="problems">
          <h2>The Problems</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 1 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={P1} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 1" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 2 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>Build a table of <code>n</code> and what is displayed on each pass.</p>

          <Code code={P2} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 2" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Then answer this:</b> 80 sits exactly on a boundary. Which branch takes it, and how do you know from the code rather than from guessing?</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 3 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={P3} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 3" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Then answer this:</b> there is no <code>ELSE</code> here and the procedure still always returns exactly one value. Explain why.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Your three answers, plus the trace table for Problem 2. Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
